codex
A simple full-Gaussian covariance pass is not competitive; it ignores fixed-weight mean shifts after the first ReLU and is badly biased on synthetic tests. The current estimator is mostly variance-limited, so I’m focusing on QMC/control-variate changes rather than replacing it with that analytic pass.
codex
One promising variance-reduction change is exact antipodal sphere pairing: evaluate each sampled direction and its negative. That preserves the correct distribution and often reduces final ReLU variance, so I’m testing it synthetically before a hidden run.
